# The accepted baseline of perf-nightly's weekly ratio check
# (.github/workflows/perf-nightly.yml): on Sundays, or on a dispatch with
# check_accepted, HEAD is re-measured against this commit on the same runner
# and the job fails on a >15% median regression. The nightly check's baseline
# moves every night; this one only moves in a reviewed PR - bump it when a
# cost is deliberately accepted, and say why in that PR (the counterpart of
# `tool/perf.sh gate --update-baseline` for counters.json).
#
# 812f8e5d = #755 (GWG Output Suite V5 conformance). It takes in #602's
# colorant buffer, whose cost is accepted in
# doc/dev-log/2026-07-25-overprint-colorant-buffer.md, and #755's own
# OutputIntent/overprint cost, which was left open (#956 took back its
# glyph-outline share; #963 cut the OutputIntent profile parse behind its
# first-page share): those fixes read as "improved" here, and anything that
# lands after #755 is judged on its own. See
# doc/dev-log/2026-09-26-perf-nightly-ratchet.md.
